### Define ServingTable Schema

Source: https://github.com/514-labs/moosestack/blob/main/apps/framework-docs-v2/content/shared/guides/performant-dashboards/phase-2-optimization.mdx

Define the schema and engine configuration for an OlapTable. Ensure orderByFields or orderByExpression is set correctly for the chosen ClickHouse engine.

```ts
import { ClickHouseEngines, Int64, OlapTable } from "@514labs/moose-lib";

interface ServingTableSchema {
  merchant_id: string;
  merchant_name: string;
  day: Date;
  total_orders: Int64;
  fulfilled_orders: Int64;
  fulfillment_rate: number;
}

export const ServingTable = new OlapTable<ServingTableSchema>(
  "<ServingTable>",
  {
    orderByFields: ["merchant_id", "day"], // This is based on the most common filter/group-by fields from your access patterns.
    engine: ClickHouseEngines.MergeTree, // Use `ClickHouseEngines.MergeTree` by default for immutable aggregates; choose another `ClickHouseEngines.*` value only when your workload needs different semantics (for example, dedup/update behavior).
  },
);
```

--------------------------------

### Configure Table orderByFields for Performance

Source: https://github.com/514-labs/moosestack/blob/main/apps/framework-docs-v2/content/moosestack/help/troubleshooting.mdx

Specify fields for ordering in OlapTable configuration to optimize query performance. Use this when experiencing slow queries due to missing or improper indexes.

```typescript
const table = new OlapTable<Data>("slow_table", {
  orderByFields: ["frequently_queried_field", "timestamp"]
});
```

```python
from moose_lib import OlapTable, OlapConfig

table = OlapTable[Data]("slow_table", OlapConfig(
    order_by_fields=["frequently_queried_field", "timestamp"]
))
```

